OL,3,ASchools 'explosive device' email not
OL,4,Aviable threat - education minister
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Education Minister Paul Givan said
OL,7,Fan email threatening that "an explosive
OL,8,Fdevice" is located within 160 schools
OL,9,Fin Northern Ireland was not being
OL,10,Ftreated as a "viable threat".
OL,12,FGivan said that the email has "caused
OL,13,Fhuge alarm" and condemned the "level of
OL,14,Fdisruption caused to young people's
OL,15,Feducation".
OL,17,FSome schools have closed after
OL,18,Freceiving the email, however others
OL,19,Fhave decided to stay open and are
OL,20,Ftaking advice from the Police Service
OL,21,Fof Northern Ireland (PSNI).
OL,23,APub: 19-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,307,300,200,140,0,100
